<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Complement and difference</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(\xi = \{x : x \text{ is a natural number}, x \le {@N@}\}\), \(A = {@dset(A)@}\) and \(B = {@dset(B)@}\).</p><p>List the elements of each set.</p><p>(a) \(A'\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>(b) \(A - B\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p><p>(c) \((A \cup B)'\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(\xi = \{1, 2, \ldots, {@N@}\}\).</p><p>(a) \(A'\) is everything in \(\xi\) that is not in \(A\): \(A' = {@dset(Ac)@}\).</p><p>(b) Start with \(A\) and remove anything that is also in \(B\), here \({@dset(I)@}\): \(A - B = {@dset(AmB)@}\).</p><p>(c) Brackets first: \(A \cup B = {@dset(AuB)@}\). Its complement is \((A \cup B)' = {@dset(UnC)@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
